<section id="states">
  <h2 id="states"><a href="#states">The same four steps, as a table</a></h2>
  <p>A universe has a short life and only four commands change it. The one worth knowing cold is the difference between <code>down</code>, which you will run every day, and <code>rm</code>, which you run once and cannot undo.</p>
  <figure class="fig wide">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 720 380" role="img" aria-labelledby="st sd">
      <title id="st">What exists after new, up, down and rm</title>
      <desc id="sd">A grid with four rows and four columns. The columns are the commands in order: new, up, down, rm. After new, the branch is made and the worktree exists, but there are no volumes and no containers. After up, all four exist and the containers are running. After down, the branch, worktree and volumes are kept and the containers are removed. After rm, the branch is kept in the clone while the worktree, the volumes and the containers are deleted.</desc>

      <text class="d-m" x="20" y="46">after</text>
      <text class="d-a" x="239" y="46" text-anchor="middle">new</text>
      <text class="d-a" x="373" y="46" text-anchor="middle">up</text>
      <text class="d-a" x="507" y="46" text-anchor="middle">down</text>
      <text class="d-a" x="641" y="46" text-anchor="middle">rm</text>
      <path class="d-line" d="M180 64H700"/>
      <path class="d-head" d="M306 64l-12-6v12zM440 64l-12-6v12zM574 64l-12-6v12z"/>

      <text class="d-t" x="20" y="115">branch</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-addr" x="180" y="86" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="239" y="115" text-anchor="middle">made</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-addr" x="314" y="86" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="373" y="115" text-anchor="middle">on it</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-addr" x="448" y="86" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="507" y="115" text-anchor="middle">on it</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-addr" x="582" y="86" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="641" y="115" text-anchor="middle">kept</text>

      <text class="d-t" x="20" y="177">worktree</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-num" x="180" y="148" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="239" y="177" text-anchor="middle">made</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-num" x="314" y="148" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="373" y="177" text-anchor="middle">yours</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-num" x="448" y="148" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="507" y="177" text-anchor="middle">yours</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-off" x="582" y="148" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-m" x="641" y="177" text-anchor="middle">deleted</text>

      <text class="d-t" x="20" y="239">your data</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-off" x="180" y="210" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-m" x="239" y="239" text-anchor="middle">none yet</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-num" x="314" y="210" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="373" y="239" text-anchor="middle">made</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-num" x="448" y="210" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="507" y="239" text-anchor="middle">kept</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-off" x="582" y="210" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-m" x="641" y="239" text-anchor="middle">deleted</text>

      <text class="d-t" x="20" y="301">containers</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-off" x="180" y="272" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-m" x="239" y="301" text-anchor="middle">none yet</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-num" x="314" y="272" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-t" x="373" y="301" text-anchor="middle">running</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-off" x="448" y="272" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-m" x="507" y="301" text-anchor="middle">removed</text>
      <rect class="d-tint-off" x="582" y="272" width="118" height="44" rx="8"/>
      <text class="d-m" x="641" y="301" text-anchor="middle">deleted</text>

      <text class="d-m" x="360" y="356" text-anchor="middle">down then up puts you back where you were</text>
    </svg>
    <p class="legend"><span><span class="sw sw-addr" aria-hidden="true"></span> in the clone, outlives the universe</span><span><span class="sw sw-num" aria-hidden="true"></span> the universe's own</span><span><span class="sw sw-off" aria-hidden="true"></span> not there</span></p>
    <figcaption><code>down</code> costs you nothing but the time to start again. <code>rm</code> takes the data and the uncommitted edits with it, and keeps only what is committed.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section id="commands">
  <h2 id="commands"><a href="#commands">The commands</a></h2>
  <div class="tw entries"><table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Command</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">What it keeps</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr><td data-l="Command"><code>start &lt;source&gt;</code></td><td data-l="Does">From nothing to something running: installs the multiverse, creates a universe if there is none, starts it, prints its addresses.</td><td data-l="Keeps">A multiverse already installed is used as it is.</td></tr>
  <tr><td data-l="Command"><code>universe new [name]</code></td><td data-l="Does">One worktree per repository on a branch that exists nowhere yet, secrets copied in from the clone, state written. Nothing is started.</td><td data-l="Keeps">Refuses rather than touch a branch that already exists.</td></tr>
  <tr><td data-l="Command"><code>universe checkout &lt;branch&gt;</code></td><td data-l="Does">The same, on a branch that already exists — to work on it or review it.</td><td data-l="Keeps">Removing the universe later never deletes the branch.</td></tr>
  <tr><td data-l="Command"><code>universe up &lt;universe&gt;</code></td><td data-l="Does">Starts it: see the order below. All apps, or only the ones you name.</td><td data-l="Keeps">Everything on disk. Safe to run again at any time.</td></tr>
  <tr><td data-l="Command"><code>universe sync [universe]</code></td><td data-l="Does">Fetches and moves each checkout forward, where that loses nothing, so a universe made last week has this week's main in it.</td><td data-l="Keeps">A checkout with uncommitted changes or commits of its own is left alone.</td></tr>
  <tr><td data-l="Command"><code>universe down &lt;universe&gt;</code></td><td data-l="Does">Takes the containers and the app networks away, and frees the memory they held.</td><td data-l="Keeps">Volumes, worktrees, state. <code>up</code> picks up where you left off.</td></tr>
  <tr><td data-l="Command"><code>universe rm &lt;universe&gt;</code></td><td data-l="Does">Destroys the universe: worktrees, containers, volumes, state. It prints what it will do and asks for the universe's name typed back.</td><td data-l="Keeps">Branches, so committed work survives. Uncommitted work in a worktree stops the removal until <code>--force</code>.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <p>Every command and flag is in <a href="../reference/cli.html">Commands</a>.</p>
</section>

<section id="up">
  <h2 id="up"><a href="#up">What <code>up</code> does, in order</a></h2>
  <p>Worth knowing because it says where a failed start stopped, and what it had already done.</p>
  <ol class="how">
    <li><strong>Checks the secrets, starts the proxy</strong>Before anything else, so a missing file leaves nothing half started. The shared proxy is started if it is not already running.</li>
    <li><strong>Reads the addresses from your compose files</strong>Labels can have changed since the universe was made, so the host rules are resolved again and kept with the universe.</li>
    <li><strong>Renders the files an app reads at boot</strong>Config written from this universe's own values, before the containers that read it exist.</li>
    <li><strong>Writes the generated fragment</strong>Proxy labels, the dropped published ports and the variables asked for by label, in a file beside your checkouts. Your own compose files are not touched.</li>
    <li><strong>Builds and starts</strong>Images are built if the app asks for it, then compose brings the services up.</li>
    <li><strong>Connects the proxy to the app's network</strong>The network exists only now, so this is the first moment the address can answer.</li>
    <li><strong>Waits, then runs the hooks</strong>Until the services with a healthcheck are healthy and the hosts that set <code>ready</code> answer — so a hook that needs the app to respond can rely on it.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Apps are independent: one that cannot start does not keep the others from it. The summary at the end says which are up and which failed, and the exit status is non-zero.</p>
</section>

<section id="many">
  <h2 id="many"><a href="#many">Living with several</a></h2>
  <p>The cost of a running universe is its containers' memory, so the usual rhythm is a handful created and one or two up. <code>universe status</code> is one line each; <code>universe ls</code> is every address.</p>
  <div class="code"><pre><span class="p">$ </span>multiversectl universe status
<span class="c">UNIVERSE    STATE     SERVICES  LAST STARTED  BRANCHES</span>
1           running   5/5       2 hours ago   feat/login
2           stopped   0/5       yesterday     main
fix/cart    created   0/5       never         fix/cart</pre></div>
  <p>A universe you are done with goes away with <code>rm</code>; <code>system prune</code> does the same across every multiverse on the machine, listing what it will remove and keeping back anything holding work that exists nowhere else. <a href="machine.html">What's on your machine</a> shows where all of it lives.</p>
</section>

